      "text": "To find $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)$ given that $\\tan x = 2$, we can use the tangent addition formula:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\n\\]\n\nWe know that $\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1$. So, substituting $\\tan x = 2$ into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{1 - 2} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\n\nSo, $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = -3$. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given value\ntan_x = 2\n\n# Using the tangent addition formula\ntan_x_plus_pi_over_4 = (tan_x + 1) / (1 - tan_x * 1)\nprint(tan_x_plus_pi_over_4)\n```\n```output\n-3.0\n```\nThe value of $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)$ is \\(\\boxed{-3}\\).",
